WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.496 --> 00:00:04.799
~ [Seasonal]

2
00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:07.136
[House]
We are condemned to useless labor.

3
00:00:07.208 --> 00:00:09.143
Fourth circle ofhell.

4
00:00:09.212 --> 00:00:13.014
Charting goes a lot faster
when you eliminate
all classic poetry.

5
00:00:13.085 --> 00:00:16.488
Writing down what we already know
to be read by nobody.

6
00:00:16.558 --> 00:00:19.393
I'm pretty sure Dante would agree
that qualifies as useless.

7
00:00:19.463 --> 00:00:21.523
You're over two weeks behind
in your charting.

8
00:00:23.069 --> 00:00:25.972
Oops. I missed.

9
00:00:26.041 --> 00:00:29.035
- What are you, eight?
- Could an eight-year-old do this?

10
00:00:30.081 --> 00:00:32.676
You'd better stop,
or it'll stick that way.

11
00:00:32.753 --> 00:00:37.193
- You have a patient in Exam One.
- Yeah, but, see, I'm off at 12:00,
and it's already five of.

12
00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.720
She's been waiting for you
since 11:00.

13
00:00:43.505 --> 00:00:48.445
Melancholy without hope.
Which circle is that?

14
00:00:53.689 --> 00:00:56.124
Hi. I'm Dr. House.

15
00:00:56.193 --> 00:01:00.394
What seems to be the problem?
Show him your hands, Augustine.

16
00:01:06.878 --> 00:01:11.147
- It-It looks like stigmata.
- Shh. Pius.

17
00:01:11.219 --> 00:01:14.816
You must be all the talk
around the "holy water'"cooler.

18
00:01:14.892 --> 00:01:18.057
Been washing a lot
of dishes recently?
I help out in the kitchen.

19
00:01:18.131 --> 00:01:22.160
- Anything new in the kitchen?
- We just got a donation
of saucepans and pots this week.

20
00:01:22.238 --> 00:01:27.110
- I unpacked and washed them.
- Should have spent your time saving souls.
It's easier on the hands.

21
00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.413
This is contact dermatitis.
You're allergic to dish soap.

22
00:01:30.486 --> 00:01:35.085
Nonsense. We've always used that soap.
Why is there a problem now?

23
00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:39.098
I've been a doctor for years.
Why do I have to keep assuring people
that I know what I'm doing?

24
00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:41.602
Aperson can become allergic
to substances...

25
00:01:41.671 --> 00:01:44.004
that they've had repeated
and prolonged exposure to.

26
00:01:45.578 --> 00:01:48.572
The good news is- free samples.

27
00:01:49.986 --> 00:01:52.615
Diphenhydramine.
It's an antihistamine.

28
00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:55.456
It'll stop the allergic reaction.

29
00:01:55.529 --> 00:01:59.058
Take one every eight hours.
It might make you feel a little sleepy.

30
00:01:59.135 --> 00:02:02.698
And get some of that
over-the-counter cortisone cream.
Thank you, Doctor.

31
00:02:02.774 --> 00:02:05.073
You want some water?
I have some tea.

32
00:02:05.145 --> 00:02:08.844
Well, you just relax for a few minutes.
That stuff works pretty fast.

33
00:02:14.628 --> 00:02:18.088
~ [Continues]
Still out by 12:00.

34
00:02:18.168 --> 00:02:21.936
How do you solve a problem
like dermatitis?
What?

35
00:02:22.007 --> 00:02:25.536
Doctor? I want to thank you
for your patience.

36
00:02:25.614 --> 00:02:30.281
She talkin' to you?
I don't know.
She's certainly looking at me.

37
00:02:30.356 --> 00:02:33.759
Ah, it's good to get
a secular diagnosis.

38
00:02:33.828 --> 00:02:37.891
The sisters tend to interpret
their illnesses as divine intervention.

39
00:02:37.969 --> 00:02:40.735
And you don't?
Then you're wearing
an awfully funny hat.

40
00:02:40.807 --> 00:02:43.368
Ooh, boy.
Excuse me.

41
00:02:43.445 --> 00:02:47.076
If I break my leg, I believe
it happened for a reason.

42
00:02:47.151 --> 00:02:49.143
I believe God wanted me
to break my leg.

43
00:02:49.221 --> 00:02:52.454
I also believe he wants me
to put a cast on it.

44
00:02:52.527 --> 00:02:54.462
Doctor.! Something's wrong.

45
00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:57.660
[Wheezing, Gasping]

46
00:03:04.649 --> 00:03:08.178
Lift up your chin.

47
00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:11.282
Sister, you're having an asthma attack.
I need you to relax.

48
00:03:11.359 --> 00:03:14.296
Roll up her sleeve, please.
I'm gonna give you epinephrine.

49
00:03:14.365 --> 00:03:17.200
- [Wheezing, Gasping Continue]
- It'll open your lungs and help you breathe.

50
00:03:31.528 --> 00:03:35.125
[Wheezing, Gasping Subside]

51
00:03:36.303 --> 00:03:39.331
What happened?
Did she take the pill?

52
00:03:39.408 --> 00:03:42.504
- Yes.
- It's probably an allergic reaction.

53
00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:45.243
She's allergic
to an anti-allergy medicine?

54
00:03:45.318 --> 00:03:47.310
You figure somebody's
out to get her?

55
00:03:47.389 --> 00:03:49.324
- How are you feeling?
- [Quietly] Better.

56
00:03:49.392 --> 00:03:52.488
I'll put you on some steroids instead.

57
00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:55.434
- Is my heart supposed to be feeling so funny?
- It's called adrenaline.

58
00:03:55.503 --> 00:03:58.736
- It makes your heart beat fast.
- [Rapid Heartbeat]

59
00:03:58.808 --> 00:04:01.779
- But not this fast.
- [Gasps]

60
00:04:01.847 --> 00:04:05.876
Get a nurse, please.
Hold on.

61
00:04:05.954 --> 00:04:08.446
Help! Somebody help us!

62
00:04:11.798 --> 00:04:14.963
Somebody get in here!

63
00:04:16.172 --> 00:04:18.972
Call a code and charge up a defibrillator.
She's got no pulse.

64
00:05:06.793 --> 00:05:09.262
[Nuns Murmuring]

65
00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:20.038
[Cuddy] You diagnosed the patient
with allergies and prescribed antihistamine.

66
00:05:20.115 --> 00:05:23.086
She went into respiratory distress,

67
00:05:23.155 --> 00:05:25.955
and you injected her
with epinephrine.

68
00:05:26.026 --> 00:05:28.120
Presumably 1 c.c.

69
00:05:28.196 --> 00:05:32.032
.1 c.c. That is the standard dose.
That is what I gave her.

70
00:05:32.103 --> 00:05:34.129
People don't go into cardiac arrest
from.1 c.c. Epinephrine.

71
00:05:34.207 --> 00:05:37.474
She must have a preexisting heart condition
that got exacerbated by the epinephrine.

72
00:05:37.546 --> 00:05:39.481
It's too bad you didn't
make a notation in the chart.

73
00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:41.485
I can make it up right now.

74
00:05:41.553 --> 00:05:44.422
The drawer has syringes with both dosages.
You could have reached for the wrong-

75
00:05:44.491 --> 00:05:46.926
- But I didn't.
- Everyone makes mistakes.

76
00:05:46.995 --> 00:05:49.055
This is why doctors pay through the nose
for malpractice insurance.

77
00:05:49.133 --> 00:05:51.659
Relax. They're not gonna sue.

78
00:05:51.736 --> 00:05:53.932
The worst they'd do
is whack my hand with a ruler.

79
00:05:54.007 --> 00:05:57.410
- And the discipline board-
are they gonna whack your hand too?
- You're gonna report me?

80
00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:01.179
- What choice do I have?
- Uh, how about not report me?

81
00:06:03.857 --> 00:06:07.818
I can justify keeping her here
for a 24-hour observation.

82
00:06:07.898 --> 00:06:10.527
If you haven't found an underlying cause
for the cardiac arrest by then,

83
00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:12.538
I will have to notify our attorneys.

84
00:06:19.217 --> 00:06:21.049
[Cameron]
Her hands were red and swollen.

85
00:06:21.121 --> 00:06:24.456
Maybe she has a skin infection. Cellulitis?
That could manifest with tachycardia.

86
00:06:24.526 --> 00:06:27.827
There's no history of fever.
Results from the C.B.C.
Didn't indicate an infection.

87
00:06:27.899 --> 00:06:31.962
The eosinophils are mildly elevated.
Sed rate's up a bit. Could we be looking
at a systemic allergic response?

88
00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:34.635
It's not allergic. Allergies don't cause
cardiac arrest like this.

89
00:06:34.711 --> 00:06:39.151
- Could be inflammation of the blood vessels.
- Vasculitis? That wouldn't give you
an elevated eosinophil count.

90
00:06:39.219 --> 00:06:41.017
Churg-Strauss vasculitis would.

91
00:06:41.088 --> 00:06:43.751
The blood vessels of the heart,
lungs and skin become inflamed,

92
00:06:43.826 --> 00:06:47.764
causing the asthma, rash and heart
problems- covers all her symptoms.

93
00:06:47.833 --> 00:06:50.166
You need a biopsy to diagnose.
Chest C.T. Would be quicker.

94
00:06:50.238 --> 00:06:53.175
The lady just came in
with a rash.

95
00:06:53.243 --> 00:06:55.178
What the hell are those?

96
00:06:55.247 --> 00:06:57.182
Candy canes.

97
00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:00.949
Candy canes?
Are you mocking me?

98
00:07:01.023 --> 00:07:04.893
No. It-It's Christmas, and l-

99
00:07:04.963 --> 00:07:08.731
I thought-
Relax. It's a joke.

100
00:07:08.804 --> 00:07:10.796
[Foreman] Isn't the prognosis
for Churg-Strauss a bit grim?

101
00:07:10.873 --> 00:07:15.074
Yeah. Untreated, only 33% of patients
survive past a year.

102
00:07:15.147 --> 00:07:18.641
Treated- five years.
Then I definitely suggest treatment.

103
00:07:18.721 --> 00:07:21.088
If it was any other attending doctor,
I'd say that he made a mistake...

104
00:07:21.158 --> 00:07:23.093
and gave her too much epinephrine.

105
00:07:23.161 --> 00:07:25.961
Saying you wouldn't say
it was my mistake...

106
00:07:26.033 --> 00:07:28.127
is saying it was my mistake.

107
00:07:29.205 --> 00:07:31.640
Everyone screws up.
Your rule.

108
00:07:31.709 --> 00:07:33.974
I think you fit within
the subset of"everyone."

109
00:07:34.047 --> 00:07:36.016
I didn't screw up.

110
00:07:36.083 --> 00:07:41.183
- Order a chest C.T. And start the sister
on prednisone- 40 milligrams T.I.D.
- The sister?

111
00:07:41.259 --> 00:07:45.858
Oh, didn't I mention?
The patient's a nun- Sister Augustine.

112
00:07:45.934 --> 00:07:48.460
[Moans]
I hate nuns.

113
00:07:50.308 --> 00:07:52.277
Who doesn't?

114
00:07:55.518 --> 00:08:00.720
~ [Upbeat]

115
00:08:04.266 --> 00:08:07.499
- [Cameron] Sister Augustine?
- We weren't watching.

116
00:08:07.571 --> 00:08:11.134
[TVTurns Off]
We were trying to see
if this is the bed control.

117
00:08:11.211 --> 00:08:13.305
Oh. Uh, this one's
the bed control.

118
00:08:13.382 --> 00:08:15.874
And that's the TV control.

119
00:08:15.953 --> 00:08:19.254
I'm Dr. Cameron.
This is Dr. Chase and Dr. Foreman.

120
00:08:19.325 --> 00:08:22.194
I haven't seen television
in over 20 years.

121
00:08:22.263 --> 00:08:24.095
Do you consider it
the work of the devil,

122
00:08:24.167 --> 00:08:26.363
or do you just not get cable
where you live?

123
00:08:27.339 --> 00:08:30.036
- Um-
- How are you feeling, Sister?

124
00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:32.511
I seem to be a little better.
They gave me some medication.

125
00:08:32.582 --> 00:08:35.017
Prednisone. It's a steroid
to help with the inflammation.

126
00:08:35.085 --> 00:08:37.520
Has Dr. House figured out what I have?

127
00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:39.718
Will I be okay?
We're not sure what's wrong yet.

128
00:08:39.794 --> 00:08:42.924
You'll have a chest C.T. Scan this afternoon
that'll help with the diagnosis.

129
00:08:42.999 --> 00:08:46.164
Dr. House is giving her medication,
and he doesn't know
what she has yet?

130
00:08:46.239 --> 00:08:49.642
Trust, Sister Pius.
It all happens for a reason.

131
00:08:49.711 --> 00:08:51.737
[Foreman]
He doesn't know what he's doing.

132
00:08:51.815 --> 00:08:54.786
The only problem that woman has
is that House grabbed
the wrong syringe.

133
00:08:54.853 --> 00:08:59.054
You don't trust him?
I don't trust a man who won't admit
he might be wrong.

134
00:08:59.127 --> 00:09:02.462
I notice you weren't so quick to tell her
she's got Churg-Strauss and only
has a couple years left.

135
00:09:02.534 --> 00:09:04.503
I don't tell patients bad news
unless it's conclusive.

136
00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:06.505
Because you know
he might be wrong.

137
00:09:06.573 --> 00:09:08.906
About Churg-Strauss. Not about
what happened in the clinic.

138
00:09:08.977 --> 00:09:12.415
[Scoffs]
What about you, Chase?
You think he's infallible too?

139
00:09:12.484 --> 00:09:16.651
All I know is, if House didn't make a mistake
and Sister Augustine has Churg-Strauss,

140
00:09:16.724 --> 00:09:19.627
he'll be self-satisfied
and our lives will be good
for a few weeks.

141
00:09:19.696 --> 00:09:23.566
If House did make a mistake,
he'll be upset and our lives
will be miserable for months.

142
00:09:23.636 --> 00:09:25.764
[Chuckles]
There is that.

143
00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:28.902
If Cuddy thinks I made a mistake,
the least she could do
is suspend me from clinic duty.

144
00:09:28.979 --> 00:09:31.814
She doesn't confuse making a mistake
with being incompetent.

145
00:09:31.884 --> 00:09:34.353
Oh, here we go- lesson time.

146
00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:38.290
I recognize that confidence
is not my short suit.

147
00:09:38.362 --> 00:09:41.093
I also recognize that I am human
and capable of error.

148
00:09:41.167 --> 00:09:44.161
So you might have
screwed this up?
No.

149
00:09:44.238 --> 00:09:47.641
So it's merely a theoretical
capacity for error.
Good point.

150
00:09:47.711 --> 00:09:50.306
Maybe there isn't one.
Maybe that's my error.

151
00:09:50.382 --> 00:09:53.615
Most people who think
as much of themselves as you do
like to talk about themselves.

152
00:09:53.688 --> 00:09:57.421
Most people don't like to listen.
So, what's wrong with you?

153
00:10:05.341 --> 00:10:07.674
[Sniffing]

154
00:10:07.746 --> 00:10:11.206
Let me guess- inflammatory bowel.

155
00:10:11.285 --> 00:10:15.053
[Sighs]
Wow. Yeah. Is it that bad?
Yes.

156
00:10:15.125 --> 00:10:18.494
It's also written on your chart.

157
00:10:18.564 --> 00:10:20.795
"Bloody diarrhea, gas, pain.

158
00:10:20.869 --> 00:10:22.895
Took sulfasalazine,
but it didn't work."

159
00:10:22.972 --> 00:10:26.068
- No. Then-Then l-
- " Next, tried steroid enemas.

160
00:10:26.144 --> 00:10:29.138
Oral corticosteroids-5-A.S.A.,
6-mercaptopurine. '"

161
00:10:29.216 --> 00:10:31.412
- I'm impressed.
- By my medical history?

162
00:10:31.486 --> 00:10:33.955
By how well
your last doctor charted.

163
00:10:34.024 --> 00:10:36.391
It's one thing to have to go
to the bathroom every hour,

164
00:10:36.462 --> 00:10:39.297
but when the kids
sit on my lap, it's-

165
00:10:39.367 --> 00:10:41.461
The store sent me home.
They're gonna fire me.

166
00:10:41.538 --> 00:10:44.509
Can't you put me back on 5-A.S.A.?
Maybe it'll work this time.
Not likely.

167
00:10:44.576 --> 00:10:48.344
I'm giving you a prescription.
It's cheap, which is good,

168
00:10:48.416 --> 00:10:50.351
because your insurance company
won't pay for it.

169
00:10:58.033 --> 00:11:01.436
- "Cogaritis"?
- Cigarettes.

170
00:11:01.505 --> 00:11:03.474
One twice a day.
No more, no less.

171
00:11:03.542 --> 00:11:05.943
Studies have shown
that cigarette smoking...

172
00:11:06.013 --> 00:11:08.676
is one of the most effective ways
to control inflammatory bowel.

173
00:11:08.752 --> 00:11:12.121
Plus it's been well established
that you look 30% cooler.

174
00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:15.650
- Are you kidding me?
- About the looking cooler, yeah.

175
00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:18.496
- The rest is true.
- Isn't it addictive and dangerous?

176
00:11:18.568 --> 00:11:22.301
Pretty much all the drugs I prescribe
are addictive and dangerous.

177
00:11:22.374 --> 00:11:24.969
The only difference with this one
is it's completely legal.

178
00:11:26.616 --> 00:11:29.085
Merry Christmas.

179
00:11:29.153 --> 00:11:32.886
[Sister Augustine]
I was talking to the nurse-Arsenio.
Do you know him?

180
00:11:32.959 --> 00:11:37.126
Not really.
He can take pictures
with his phone.

181
00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:40.660
Cool.
That woman from the lab
was interesting too.

182
00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:43.870
She studied astrophysics
before becoming a nurse.

183
00:11:43.945 --> 00:11:47.906
You know the staff
better than I do.
I love to hear all about people.

184
00:11:47.985 --> 00:11:51.115
- Yet you live in a monastery.
- It's where I serve our Lord
and the world best.

185
00:11:51.191 --> 00:11:54.959
Our Lord maybe.
The rest of the world,
on the other hand,

186
00:11:55.031 --> 00:11:58.799
- would probably get more
out of feeding the homeless or-
- Healing the sick?

187
00:11:58.871 --> 00:12:02.832
As an example, yeah.
Did you always want
to be a doctor?

188
00:12:02.911 --> 00:12:06.974
Always.
You always want to be a nun?
My parents died when I was six.

189
00:12:07.052 --> 00:12:10.683
I was raised in a foster home
run by the Church.

190
00:12:10.758 --> 00:12:14.787
When I was 18, I went to the monastery,
where they let me take my vows.

191
00:12:14.866 --> 00:12:18.065
I've known no other life,
and I haven't wanted to.

192
00:12:18.137 --> 00:12:21.666
[Foreman On Speaker]
Okay, Sister. We need you
to lie as still as possible.

193
00:12:21.744 --> 00:12:23.736
If you get scared,
just let us know.

194
00:12:23.814 --> 00:12:26.614
As Jonah said from inside the whale,

195
00:12:26.685 --> 00:12:30.954
"When I had lost all hope,
I turned my thoughts to the Lord. '"

196
00:12:31.027 --> 00:12:34.590
- Well, she's got God on her side.
- [Cameron] I don't believe in God.

197
00:12:34.666 --> 00:12:38.001
You're not even a little agnostic?
[Sister Augustine On Speaker]
Is it supposed to smell funny?

198
00:12:38.072 --> 00:12:41.976
Someone ralphed in there this morning.
We cleaned it up, but-

199
00:12:42.046 --> 00:12:45.449
- It's normal, Sister.
It's just a few more minutes.
- Mm.

200
00:12:45.518 --> 00:12:48.648
I believe in a higher order
that's in control of what happens,

201
00:12:48.723 --> 00:12:51.523
but not one, anthropomorphic entity
called "God'"...

202
00:12:51.596 --> 00:12:53.792
that's concerned with
the everyday workings of you and me.

203
00:12:53.866 --> 00:12:56.632
What else is there to control
but the everyday workings of you and me?

204
00:12:56.704 --> 00:12:58.673
It's always about you, Foreman.

205
00:12:58.741 --> 00:13:00.539
What are you talking about-
the trees, the fish?

206
00:13:00.611 --> 00:13:02.580
Should they be the ones that think
it's all about them?

207
00:13:02.648 --> 00:13:04.708
What about you, Chase?
Do you believe in God?

208
00:13:06.855 --> 00:13:11.227
I believe Sister Augustine
has no vascular pathology,
which means no Churg-Strauss.

209
00:13:11.296 --> 00:13:13.697
Which means House made a mistake.
No, not necessarily.

210
00:13:13.767 --> 00:13:17.569
It could be something else-
thyrotoxicosis or a carcinoid.
I don't get you.

211
00:13:17.641 --> 00:13:21.374
You don't believe in God,
but you're willing to put
complete faith in one man?

212
00:13:21.447 --> 00:13:24.782
[Sister Augustine]
Please. The smell.
Let's get her out of there.

213
00:13:26.322 --> 00:13:28.291
[Gasping]
I'm coming, Sister.
I gotcha.

214
00:13:28.359 --> 00:13:30.794
[Gasping]
Please. The smell.
I'm comin'.

215
00:13:30.863 --> 00:13:33.094
I'm gonna be sick.
There's no smell.

216
00:13:33.167 --> 00:13:38.437
No. God. Oh! It's Jesus.
It's Jesus!

217
00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:40.945
[Crying]
He's coming for me!

218
00:13:41.015 --> 00:13:43.484
He's burning me with his touch!

219
00:13:43.551 --> 00:13:45.417
Let's get her on some Ativan.

220
00:13:45.489 --> 00:13:49.325
The smells, religious visions-
it's symptomatic of temporal lobe swelling.

221
00:13:49.396 --> 00:13:51.991
- We don't want her to-
- She's seizing.

222
00:13:52.067 --> 00:13:54.764
- Jaw block!
- Help me get her on her side.

223
00:13:57.208 --> 00:14:00.475
- Religious visions?
- Yeah. And next comes-

224
00:14:07.627 --> 00:14:10.028
Patient tested positive
for herpetic encephalitis.

225
00:14:10.098 --> 00:14:12.659
- What's that tell us?
- Her immune system
is severely compromised.

226
00:14:12.736 --> 00:14:16.299
Oh, I know. Prednisone
compromises the immune system.

227
00:14:16.375 --> 00:14:21.645
- Isn't that the medicine that you gave her
for that thing she doesn't have?
- Yeah, that- Hey.

228
00:14:21.717 --> 00:14:25.884
- I'm thinking that's a trick question.
- Her immune system
is severely compromised.

229
00:14:25.958 --> 00:14:30.864
- Two doses of prednisone wouldn't do that.
- Are you hanging your diagnosis on an adverb?

230
00:14:30.934 --> 00:14:35.965
- In 10 seconds, I'm going to announce that
I gave her the wrong dose in the clinic.
- You're gonna admit negligence?

231
00:14:36.043 --> 00:14:39.037
Unless you leave the room.
If you stay, you'll have to testify.

232
00:14:39.115 --> 00:14:42.644
Five, four,

233
00:14:42.721 --> 00:14:45.316
three, two-

234
00:14:45.391 --> 00:14:47.360
So, there I was in the clinic, drunk.

235
00:14:47.429 --> 00:14:49.489
[Laughs]
I opened the drawer,
closed my eyes,

236
00:14:49.566 --> 00:14:51.728
take the first syringe I can find-

237
00:14:53.606 --> 00:14:56.441
So, what are the options
for a compromised immune system?

238
00:14:56.512 --> 00:15:01.646
Mixed connective tissue disease.
It'd explain why she was feeling better
on the prednisone.

239
00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:04.748
Sure. She was feeling better
right up to the moment
it almost killed her.

240
00:15:04.826 --> 00:15:07.523
On the other hand,
it explains the symptoms-

241
00:15:07.597 --> 00:15:10.123
swollen hands, pulmonary problems,
cardiac problems.

242
00:15:10.202 --> 00:15:12.103
It all fits.
Except her A.N.A. Was normal.

243
00:15:12.172 --> 00:15:14.903
- So redraw the blood.
- But the treatment is corticosteroids-

244
00:15:14.976 --> 00:15:17.207
prednisone- and we can't go there
because of the encephalitis.

245
00:15:17.281 --> 00:15:21.242
Then we'll treat it with something
that modulates the immune system
but doesn't suppress it-

246
00:15:21.321 --> 00:15:24.121
hyperbaric oxygen chamber.

247
00:15:24.193 --> 00:15:28.963
There's no protocol for putting a patient
in a high-pressure oxygen room
to treat auto-immune problems.

248
00:15:29.034 --> 00:15:31.401
Oh, you people.
Always with the protocols.

249
00:15:32.874 --> 00:15:36.607
Prep the nun
and discontinue the prednisone.

250
00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:45.286
I am both amused and annoyed...

251
00:15:45.362 --> 00:15:47.854
that you think I should be
less stubborn than you are.

252
00:15:49.302 --> 00:15:52.535
You are aware
of the Hippocratic oath, right?

253
00:15:52.608 --> 00:15:56.877
The one that starts, "First, do no harm,"
then goes on to tell us no abortions,
no seductions,

254
00:15:56.949 --> 00:15:59.646
and definitely no cutting
of those who labor beneath the stone?

255
00:15:59.721 --> 00:16:01.656
Yeah. I took a read once.
Wasn't impressed.

256
00:16:01.724 --> 00:16:05.787
Hyperbaric treatments could cause
oxygen toxicity- lung and eye damage.

257
00:16:05.864 --> 00:16:08.356
Every treatment has its dangers.
Which is why we only treat...

258
00:16:08.435 --> 00:16:11.064
if we're convinced the patient
actually needs the treatment.

259
00:16:11.140 --> 00:16:13.803
I'm convinced.
You're not.

260
00:16:15.014 --> 00:16:17.347
Question is, what are you
gonna do about it? Hmm?

261
00:16:20.423 --> 00:16:23.485
I have an opening Thursday at 3:00.
Do you have a fourth?

262
00:16:24.497 --> 00:16:27.160
Is he any good?
[Door Opens]

263
00:16:27.235 --> 00:16:29.227
Can I call you right back? Okay.

264
00:16:31.142 --> 00:16:33.134
What's up?

265
00:16:36.083 --> 00:16:39.919
[Chase]
The pressure will force the oxygen
into your system, saturate your blood.

266
00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:43.052
It will enhance white cell activity,
reduce the inflammation.

267
00:16:43.128 --> 00:16:46.258
And that will help with this
mixed connective tissue disease?

268
00:16:46.335 --> 00:16:49.500
We'll be doing about 10 treatments,
and then we'll reevaluate.

269
00:16:49.573 --> 00:16:52.942
[Sister Augustine]
The last treatment with prednisone
caused the seizures, right?

270
00:16:53.013 --> 00:16:56.883
How confident is Dr. House about this?

271
00:16:56.952 --> 00:16:59.718
[Cameron]
That you reacted so strongly
to the prednisone let us know...

272
00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:01.884
that you had an underlying problem
with your immune system.

273
00:17:01.961 --> 00:17:05.421
I guess it was a blessing... of sorts.

274
00:17:09.842 --> 00:17:12.505
[Man On TV] So, who's your favorite
reindeer, Nurse Arnold?

275
00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:14.515
Rudolph.
I would've thought
it was Vixen.

276
00:17:14.583 --> 00:17:17.952
What are you implying?
Nothing.

277
00:17:18.022 --> 00:17:20.651
But I saw you at the Christmas party
with Dr. Riles...

278
00:17:20.727 --> 00:17:23.162
and Dr. Jorkins
and Nurse Crandall.

279
00:17:23.232 --> 00:17:25.258
[Nurse]
I was just doing
some Christmas dancing.

280
00:17:25.335 --> 00:17:29.832
- This is a chapel, a house of prayer.
- [TVContinues, Indistinct]

281
00:17:29.909 --> 00:17:32.037
House of prayer? Huh.

282
00:17:32.113 --> 00:17:34.048
That explains the good reception.

283
00:17:34.117 --> 00:17:37.179
Also why nobody's ever here.

284
00:17:39.292 --> 00:17:41.386
I need to talk with you, Dr. House.

285
00:17:41.463 --> 00:17:44.593
Sister Augustine believes in things
that aren't real.

286
00:17:45.904 --> 00:17:48.169
I thought that was a job requirement
for you people.

287
00:17:48.241 --> 00:17:52.738
She's been known to lie
to get sympathy.

288
00:17:52.816 --> 00:17:55.081
She's a hypochondriac.

289
00:17:55.153 --> 00:17:59.114
So you're warning me that I may
be treating a nonexistent ailment.

290
00:17:59.194 --> 00:18:01.686
Sore throats, joint pains.

291
00:18:01.765 --> 00:18:04.634
There's always something wrong,
and there's never a reason for it.

292
00:18:04.703 --> 00:18:06.729
Mother Superior plays right into it-

293
00:18:06.806 --> 00:18:09.503
lets Augustine off work duties,

294
00:18:09.578 --> 00:18:12.344
treating her as fragile, special.

295
00:18:12.416 --> 00:18:15.216
That must make you angry.

296
00:18:15.288 --> 00:18:17.280
It bothers me.

297
00:18:17.358 --> 00:18:19.827
It's not really
in Augustine's best interests.

298
00:18:23.503 --> 00:18:26.872
You want some?

299
00:18:26.941 --> 00:18:29.935
I shouldn't.

300
00:18:34.722 --> 00:18:37.784
I guess you gotta
be good at reading people
to be a good infirmarian, huh?

301
00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:40.888
Mm. Mm-hmm.

302
00:18:40.965 --> 00:18:43.594
So, we've got pride, anger, envy,
gluttony-

303
00:18:44.972 --> 00:18:48.171
That's four out of seven deadly sins
in under two minutes.

304
00:18:48.245 --> 00:18:51.239
Do you people keep records of these things?
Is there a "Cathlympics"?

305
00:18:53.420 --> 00:18:56.414
They say you have a gift.
They like to talk.

306
00:18:56.493 --> 00:19:00.022
- You hide behind your intelligence.
- Yeah. That's pretty stupid.

307
00:19:00.098 --> 00:19:03.092
And you make jokes because you're
afraid to take anything seriously.

308
00:19:03.170 --> 00:19:05.435
Because if you take things seriously,
they matter.

309
00:19:05.508 --> 00:19:08.604
And if they matter-
When things go wrong,
I get hurt.

310
00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:11.776
- I'm not tough. I'm vulnerable.
- I barely know you.

311
00:19:11.852 --> 00:19:15.051
And I don't know if I'm right.
I just hope I am.

312
00:19:15.124 --> 00:19:17.525
Because the alternative is...

313
00:19:17.596 --> 00:19:20.065
you really are as miserable
as you seem to be.

314
00:19:22.972 --> 00:19:26.102
You know, from the way
you're looking at me right now,

315
00:19:26.177 --> 00:19:28.146
I'd say you just hit number five.

316
00:19:29.483 --> 00:19:31.850
Lust.

317
00:19:43.774 --> 00:19:47.041
[TVTurns On]
Dr. Brown, I love you too.

318
00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:52.219
[Air Hissing]

319
00:19:52.288 --> 00:19:54.519
[Vacuum Releases]

320
00:19:55.595 --> 00:19:58.896
How are you feeling?
A little weak.

321
00:19:58.967 --> 00:20:01.630
- That's from the oxygen.
- My mouth is dry.

322
00:20:01.705 --> 00:20:05.074
Okay. Well, uh, I'll get you
some of your tea.

323
00:20:07.281 --> 00:20:11.083
Mixed connective tissue disease?
Her A.N.A. Is barely elevated.

324
00:20:11.155 --> 00:20:13.886
Thanks for checking up on her.
Good to know you got my back.

325
00:20:13.959 --> 00:20:17.624
O2 sat's down to 83.
Pulmonary problems,
breathing problems.

326
00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:19.726
Irritation from the oxygen
is typical.

327
00:20:19.803 --> 00:20:22.706
She comes in with a rash,
and you put her into cardiac arrest.

328
00:20:22.774 --> 00:20:24.936
[Sighs]
That well just never
runs dry, does it?

329
00:20:25.012 --> 00:20:28.506
If there was no underlying problem,
why is she still having
the rapid heart rate?

330
00:20:28.585 --> 00:20:31.214
Maybe from the herpetic encephalitis
caused by you giving her prednisone.

331
00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:33.486
Her reaction is a symptom,
not an error.

332
00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:35.722
There's always an explanation,
isn't there?
Yes, there is.

333
00:20:35.797 --> 00:20:38.734
And if this one doesn't work,
we'll find another.
But never one involving you screwing up.

334
00:20:38.802 --> 00:20:40.794
One that fits all the facts.

335
00:20:40.873 --> 00:20:44.174
Look, we obviously have
a difference of opinion,
and that's fine.

336
00:20:44.245 --> 00:20:47.842
But, unfortunately, I've used up
all the time I budgeted today
for banging my head against a wall.

337
00:20:47.918 --> 00:20:51.356
I'm gonna do you the biggest favor
one doctor can do for another.

338
00:20:51.424 --> 00:20:54.224
I am gonna stop you
from killing your patient.

339
00:20:54.295 --> 00:20:56.696
You're off the case.

340
00:21:14.999 --> 00:21:17.195
We're gonna treat the symptoms.
Not the underlying condition?

341
00:21:17.269 --> 00:21:19.795
There is no underlying condition.
What's her status?

342
00:21:19.873 --> 00:21:21.933
The sister's breathing
is labored.

343
00:21:22.011 --> 00:21:24.412
Pneumonitis
from the hyperbaric chamber.

344
00:21:24.481 --> 00:21:27.850
Put her on 40% oxygen
until her O2 sats increase.
B.U.N. And creatinine's rising.

345
00:21:27.921 --> 00:21:30.482
A.L.T. And A.S.T. Twice the normal range.

346
00:21:30.559 --> 00:21:34.156
Could be from the hypotensive episode.
Let's follow them with labs.

347
00:21:34.232 --> 00:21:37.897
She still has the rash and joint pain
she came in with.

348
00:21:37.971 --> 00:21:41.500
Order a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory.
When we were looking at the differential
diagnosis with Dr. House,

349
00:21:41.578 --> 00:21:44.481
we were considering-
I don't need to hear
what Dr. House was considering.

350
00:21:44.549 --> 00:21:47.987
All of this woman's symptoms can be
traced to Dr. House's considerations.

351
00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:52.595
Okay.

352
00:21:52.663 --> 00:21:55.155
Let's just get this patient healthy.

353
00:21:55.235 --> 00:21:57.966
I want her going out the front door
and not the back.

354
00:21:59.976 --> 00:22:01.911
Hey, it's not like
I betrayed him.

355
00:22:01.980 --> 00:22:04.449
Cuddy would have found out about
the hyperbaric treatments eventually.

356
00:22:04.517 --> 00:22:06.679
You did what you
thought you had to.
[Sighs]

357
00:22:23.149 --> 00:22:25.084
Can't get enough
of this place, huh?

358
00:22:26.889 --> 00:22:28.824
Came for my stethoscope.

359
00:22:28.892 --> 00:22:31.920
So I shouldn't read too much
into the fact that you
were looking for it...

360
00:22:31.998 --> 00:22:33.990
in the drawer
with the epinephrine syringes in it?

361
00:22:36.105 --> 00:22:39.167
Okay. Yeah, I'd like to clear
my reputation.

362
00:22:39.244 --> 00:22:42.807
Oh, right. I forgot how much
you care about what people think.

363
00:22:42.884 --> 00:22:45.719
Prescribing cigarettes
for inflammatory bowel?

364
00:22:45.789 --> 00:22:47.883
That's, uh-They cause
lung cancer, you know.

365
00:22:47.959 --> 00:22:50.725
You know why they have ribbons
for breast cancer,

366
00:22:50.797 --> 00:22:54.565
colorectal cancer, prostate cancer-
and not for lung cancer?

367
00:22:54.637 --> 00:22:56.606
They ran out of colors?

368
00:22:56.674 --> 00:22:59.235
It's because people
blame lung cancer patients.

369
00:22:59.312 --> 00:23:01.247
They smoke. They screwed up.
They deserve to die.

370
00:23:01.315 --> 00:23:04.411
The reason people die
from lung cancer is guilt.

371
00:23:04.487 --> 00:23:07.322
Huh. Well, guilt
does a lot of damage.

372
00:23:09.296 --> 00:23:11.663
You said that
with great significance.

373
00:23:11.734 --> 00:23:15.570
You're not here to find your stethoscope.
You're not here to clear your reputation.

374
00:23:15.640 --> 00:23:19.807
You're here because you're having doubts.
You might have screwed up.

375
00:23:19.881 --> 00:23:22.476
I'm here because, if I'm right,
Cuddy is killing that patient.

376
00:23:22.552 --> 00:23:24.919
Okay. But if you're wrong?

377
00:23:27.394 --> 00:23:29.329
Then she's saving her.
Fine.

378
00:23:29.398 --> 00:23:31.799
You're gonna have to go through
every record of every patient...

379
00:23:31.868 --> 00:23:34.360
who's been through this clinic
in the last two days.

380
00:23:34.439 --> 00:23:37.604
And you're gonna have to hope
that those records can be trusted.

381
00:23:37.678 --> 00:23:39.874
Which, by the way, yours can't.

382
00:23:50.600 --> 00:23:53.730
These pills will help your kidneys
function a little better, Sister.

383
00:24:00.751 --> 00:24:02.686
Get your wrist?

384
00:24:04.491 --> 00:24:06.892
What's that?

385
00:24:06.962 --> 00:24:09.329
104.

386
00:24:09.400 --> 00:24:12.394
Is that good?
It's fine.

387
00:24:13.674 --> 00:24:17.612
You're a lousy liar, Dr. Chase.
[Pager Beeping]

388
00:24:23.524 --> 00:24:26.359
I have to get this.
Excuse me.

389
00:24:26.429 --> 00:24:28.898
[Door Opens]

390
00:24:28.967 --> 00:24:31.198
My mother's been dead
for 10 years.

391
00:24:32.339 --> 00:24:34.308
But she's always with you in spirit.

392
00:24:34.376 --> 00:24:36.470
What do you know about the nun?
Which one?

393
00:24:36.546 --> 00:24:39.984
The cute one.
I think she likes me.

394
00:24:40.052 --> 00:24:43.785
- The sick one, obviously.
- Her parents died when she was a child.

395
00:24:43.859 --> 00:24:46.454
She's been with the Church
ever since.
What's she lying about?

396
00:24:46.531 --> 00:24:49.000
- Why do you say that?
- I always say that.

397
00:24:49.068 --> 00:24:51.765
And the old nun thinks the sick nun
is a big fat nun liar.

398
00:24:51.840 --> 00:24:54.606
You know nuns.
What do you think?
I don't know nuns.

399
00:24:54.678 --> 00:24:57.672
You hate nuns. You can't hate someone
if you don't know them.

400
00:24:57.750 --> 00:25:00.311
Know any Nazis?
Maybe I hate them on principle.

401
00:25:01.890 --> 00:25:04.587
I have a theory about
what makes good boys good.

402
00:25:04.662 --> 00:25:07.997
It's not because
of some moral imperative.

403
00:25:08.067 --> 00:25:10.400
Good boys have the fear of God
put into them.

404
00:25:10.471 --> 00:25:13.533
Catholic Church specializes
in that kind of training-

405
00:25:13.611 --> 00:25:16.605
to make good boys
afraid of divine retribution,

406
00:25:16.683 --> 00:25:18.811
so they'll do
what their daddies tell them-

407
00:25:18.886 --> 00:25:22.790
like, for example, going into medical school
when it's the last thing they wanna do.

408
00:25:22.859 --> 00:25:24.794
What do you think?

409
00:25:26.266 --> 00:25:28.997
I think, if she did have a secret,
her boss would know.

410
00:25:31.575 --> 00:25:34.512
[Bells Tolling]

411
00:25:34.580 --> 00:25:38.074
Did you paint or put in
new carpets recently?
No.

412
00:25:38.152 --> 00:25:40.348
Any way she could have
got access to drugs?

413
00:25:40.423 --> 00:25:44.486
We lock all our medications in the infirmary,
and we don't keep prescription drugs here.

414
00:25:44.564 --> 00:25:48.833
Why haven't you asked Sister Augustine
about these things directly?

415
00:25:48.904 --> 00:25:51.841
I've found that when you want
to know the truth about someone,

416
00:25:51.909 --> 00:25:54.675
that someone is probably
the last person you should ask.

417
00:25:54.749 --> 00:25:57.378
Ah. And have you been speaking
to Sister Eucharist?

418
00:25:57.452 --> 00:26:01.083
She ratted out her fellow sister
pretty quickly.
Oh.

419
00:26:01.159 --> 00:26:03.390
If I were you, I'd have her repeat
a year of nun school.

420
00:26:03.463 --> 00:26:06.798
[Laughing]
Well, becoming a nun
doesn't make you a saint.

421
00:26:06.869 --> 00:26:09.304
Becoming a doctor
doesn't make you a healer.

422
00:26:09.373 --> 00:26:13.209
And just because we live in a monastery,
and we spend most of our time in prayer,

423
00:26:13.280 --> 00:26:16.149
doesn't mean we don't
find time for drama.

424
00:26:16.218 --> 00:26:18.084
So, what is the sick one's drama?

425
00:26:18.156 --> 00:26:22.892
Sister Augustine lived in Catholic
foster care until she came to us.

426
00:26:22.963 --> 00:26:24.898
[Teakettle Whistling]

427
00:26:24.967 --> 00:26:27.664
- Tea?
- Sure.

428
00:26:30.844 --> 00:26:33.473
Do all of you lie?

429
00:26:33.549 --> 00:26:36.075
It's a good strategy, ; it's simpler
when you all tell the same lie.

430
00:26:36.153 --> 00:26:39.124
She has not spent her entire life
as a good Catholic.

431
00:26:39.192 --> 00:26:43.130
When she had a cardiac arrest,
I had to open her blouse to do C.P.R.

432
00:26:43.199 --> 00:26:46.193
And I learned two things:
Nuns can have nice breasts,

433
00:26:46.270 --> 00:26:50.767
and she has a tattoo on her shoulder-
of a skunk.

434
00:26:50.845 --> 00:26:54.943
Now, maybe
it's the sacred skunk ofJoseph,

435
00:26:55.018 --> 00:26:58.285
but, as far as I know,
Catholic foster care and monasteries...

436
00:26:58.358 --> 00:27:01.158
do not keep tattoo parlors
in their refectories.

437
00:27:01.230 --> 00:27:03.927
We consider that our life begins...

438
00:27:04.001 --> 00:27:06.527
when we put on our habits
and take our vows.

439
00:27:08.242 --> 00:27:12.203
- What happens before then-
- Is irrelevant to you,
but it's relevant to me.

440
00:27:16.356 --> 00:27:19.657
Sister Augustine went into foster care
when she was six years old,

441
00:27:19.728 --> 00:27:22.323
but she left when she was 12.

442
00:27:22.399 --> 00:27:25.268
She lived on the streets.
She got into drugs.

443
00:27:26.641 --> 00:27:28.735
When she was 15,
she became pregnant.

444
00:27:28.811 --> 00:27:30.746
Tried to self-abort.

445
00:27:30.815 --> 00:27:33.752
She lost the child.
She became ill.

446
00:27:33.820 --> 00:27:35.755
We took her in
when she came back.

447
00:27:35.823 --> 00:27:40.354
If we had thought
it was medically relevant,
we would have told you.

448
00:27:42.434 --> 00:27:44.460
It's not.

449
00:27:52.585 --> 00:27:56.387
This tea is delicious.
Local herbs?

450
00:27:57.393 --> 00:28:00.660
Any change
with the medication?
Yes. She's getting worse.

451
00:28:00.732 --> 00:28:04.033
Lung function's deteriorating.
B.U.N. And creatinine
continuing to rise.

452
00:28:04.105 --> 00:28:06.597
She's starting to run a fever,
and the rash is spreading.

453
00:28:06.676 --> 00:28:08.907
At this rate, she's not
gonna make Christmas.
Maybe House is right.

454
00:28:08.980 --> 00:28:11.313
Maybe there is an underlying condition
that explains the symptoms.

455
00:28:11.384 --> 00:28:13.979
Something we haven't considered.
Like what?

456
00:28:14.055 --> 00:28:16.183
It could be a metabolic disorder.
Specifically?

457
00:28:16.260 --> 00:28:18.195
Might be genetic.
Specifically?

458
00:28:18.263 --> 00:28:20.596
I'm just saying-
You're just saying
you think House is right.

459
00:28:20.667 --> 00:28:23.193
Might be right.
Of course he might be right.

460
00:28:23.272 --> 00:28:26.107
It might be the hand of God at work.
Don't say it's something else...

461
00:28:26.176 --> 00:28:28.475
unless you've got
something concrete to offer.

462
00:28:30.784 --> 00:28:32.980
What's this, hemlock?

463
00:28:33.055 --> 00:28:36.356
I'm gonna do you the biggest favor
one doctor can do another.

464
00:28:36.427 --> 00:28:38.362
I'm gonna stop you
from killing your patient.

465
00:28:39.733 --> 00:28:43.728
It's figwort tea-
great for that little pick-me-up
we're all looking for in the morning.

466
00:28:43.807 --> 00:28:47.404
Opens the lungs,
increases the blood pressure,
stimulates the heart.

467
00:28:47.479 --> 00:28:51.383
Unfortunately, if you then get injected
with even.1 c.c. Of epinephrine-

468
00:28:51.453 --> 00:28:54.014
instant cardiac arrest.

469
00:28:55.093 --> 00:28:57.358
- Still, what the hell, it tastes great.
- Sister Augustine-

470
00:28:57.431 --> 00:28:59.923
Has been drinking it religiously,
so to speak.

471
00:29:00.002 --> 00:29:02.996
And if you take the cardiac arrest
out of the equation-

472
00:29:03.074 --> 00:29:07.275
All the rest of the symptoms
can be explained by a severe
long-term allergic reaction.

473
00:29:07.348 --> 00:29:09.510
Well, that's what Cameron
said in the beginning.

474
00:29:09.585 --> 00:29:13.182
Yes, she did. Well done.

475
00:29:13.257 --> 00:29:18.459
But your unwillingness
to stick by your diagnosis
almost killed this woman.

476
00:29:18.533 --> 00:29:21.094
Take a lesson from Foreman-
stand up for what you believe.

477
00:29:22.641 --> 00:29:26.808
Okay. Let's go figure out
how to save a nun.

478
00:29:26.881 --> 00:29:28.907
Damned if you do,
damned if you don't.

479
00:29:30.388 --> 00:29:32.323
[House]
Because it's been untreated for so long,

480
00:29:32.391 --> 00:29:34.917
it's gone from a simple " watery eyes,
scratchy throat" allergy...

481
00:29:34.995 --> 00:29:37.328
to a whopping
"I'm gonna kick your ass" allergy-

482
00:29:37.400 --> 00:29:41.395
compromising her immune system,
diminishing her ability to heal
and breaking down her organ systems.

483
00:29:41.473 --> 00:29:44.911
So, what's the source?
[Chase]
The dish soap.

484
00:29:44.979 --> 00:29:48.007
No. The symptoms persisted days
after the dish-washing episode.

485
00:29:48.085 --> 00:29:51.284
It's gotta be something she's been
exposed to here in the hospital
as well as the monastery.

486
00:29:51.357 --> 00:29:53.519
[Foreman]
What about the tea?
It caused her arrhythmia.

487
00:29:53.594 --> 00:29:55.529
Could be, but it's not definitive.

488
00:29:55.597 --> 00:29:58.397
[Chase] We'll skin-test for allergens.
[Cameron]
Not yet. She's too reactive.

489
00:29:58.469 --> 00:30:00.404
She tests positive to everything.
We need to stabilize her-

490
00:30:00.473 --> 00:30:03.569
isolate her from all possible allergens-
give her system a rest.

491
00:30:03.645 --> 00:30:05.580
[Chase]
Get her in a clean room.
[House] Okay.

492
00:30:05.648 --> 00:30:07.776
Then gradually introduce allergens
and see how she responds.

493
00:30:07.852 --> 00:30:10.721
When she reacts to something,
we'll know that's what's killing her.

494
00:30:12.193 --> 00:30:15.130
There you go.
No television, no books.

495
00:30:15.198 --> 00:30:17.463
- Not even my Bible?
- I'm afraid not.

496
00:30:17.535 --> 00:30:19.902
This room has filtered air,
filtered water.

497
00:30:19.973 --> 00:30:23.843
You even have silk sheets-
very decadent and hypoallergenic.

498
00:30:23.913 --> 00:30:26.382
You should be feeling better here.

499
00:30:26.451 --> 00:30:28.818
[Monitor Beeping]

500
00:30:28.888 --> 00:30:32.053
We'll be back to check on you
in a little while.

501
00:30:32.128 --> 00:30:36.329
Can the other sisters
come in and pray with me?

502
00:30:37.604 --> 00:30:40.370
It'd be better if you
don't have any visitors.

503
00:30:40.442 --> 00:30:43.037
Once we isolate
what's causing your allergy,

504
00:30:43.113 --> 00:30:45.048
then we can be a little more lax.

505
00:30:47.487 --> 00:30:49.422
[Whimpers]

506
00:30:49.490 --> 00:30:51.982
[Crying]

507
00:30:54.833 --> 00:30:58.703
[Whimpering]
L-I can pray with you.

508
00:30:58.773 --> 00:31:01.504
I don't wanna die.

509
00:31:01.578 --> 00:31:03.740
[Crying]
Why has he left me?

510
00:31:13.732 --> 00:31:15.758
I was in seminary school.

511
00:31:17.840 --> 00:31:20.105
They asked us once
what our favorite passage was.

512
00:31:20.177 --> 00:31:23.342
I chose First Peter,
chapter one, verse seven.

513
00:31:25.587 --> 00:31:29.423
"These trials only test your faith
to see whether or not
it is strong and pure.

514
00:31:29.493 --> 00:31:34.798
Your faith is being tested,
as fire tests gold and purifies it."

515
00:31:34.869 --> 00:31:38.272
"And your faith is far more precious
to the Lord than mere gold.

516
00:31:38.342 --> 00:31:40.675
"So if your faith remains strong
after being tested,

517
00:31:40.746 --> 00:31:45.379
"it will bring you much praise
and glory and honor...

518
00:31:46.856 --> 00:31:48.791
on the day of his return."

519
00:31:48.860 --> 00:31:50.988
He hasn't left you.

520
00:31:51.063 --> 00:31:54.967
[Laughing, Crying]

521
00:31:55.037 --> 00:31:58.065
The only thing in the way of you
knowing he's there is your fear.

522
00:31:58.142 --> 00:32:03.846
You have a choice- faith or fear.
That's the test.

523
00:32:03.920 --> 00:32:06.082
Choosing faith
doesn't mean I won't die.

524
00:32:06.156 --> 00:32:08.318
But it will affect
how you experience your death...

525
00:32:08.394 --> 00:32:10.989
and, therefore, your life.

526
00:32:11.065 --> 00:32:12.829
It's up to you.

527
00:32:12.901 --> 00:32:15.895
Why did you leave seminary school?

528
00:32:17.643 --> 00:32:20.238
That test.

529
00:32:20.315 --> 00:32:22.910
You passed. I didn't.

530
00:32:24.322 --> 00:32:27.555
We'll call you if anything changes.
Will she be all right?

531
00:32:27.627 --> 00:32:31.565
As long as she's not exposed
to anything that can aggravate
her allergy, she'll be fine.

532
00:32:33.003 --> 00:32:36.964
- I need some help in here!
- [Sister Augustine Gasping]

533
00:32:39.548 --> 00:32:42.610
Screw the procedure!
She's in anaphylactic shock!

534
00:32:42.686 --> 00:32:44.917
No way. She's in a damn clean room.
You kidding me?

535
00:32:44.991 --> 00:32:46.926
Get in here!

536
00:32:46.994 --> 00:32:51.627
[Chase]. 1 c.c. Of epi.
[Foreman]
We've got to intubate.

537
00:32:51.702 --> 00:32:54.137
[Cameron]
I got it. Get the ambu bag.

538
00:33:05.893 --> 00:33:08.362
[Sister Augustine Gasps]
I'm in.

539
00:33:14.241 --> 00:33:16.506
[Oxygen Pulsing]

540
00:33:17.747 --> 00:33:20.444
[Monitor Beeping]

541
00:33:20.519 --> 00:33:23.011
Breathing's stabilized.

542
00:33:24.391 --> 00:33:26.860
It's a clean room.

543
00:33:34.776 --> 00:33:37.245
[House]
How do you get an allergic reaction
in a clean room?

544
00:33:39.184 --> 00:33:43.213
Maybe it was the preservatives
in the I.V.?
Checked that.

545
00:33:43.291 --> 00:33:45.852
Latex tubing?
Checked that.
Checked everything.

546
00:33:45.929 --> 00:33:50.631
Well, it could be mast cell leukemia.
It can cause anaphylaxis.

547
00:33:50.704 --> 00:33:56.203
I checked the blood levels,
and it's not eosinophilia
or idiopathic anaphylaxis.

548
00:33:56.280 --> 00:33:59.410
Maybe it's just divine will.

549
00:33:59.486 --> 00:34:01.978
It's not my will.

550
00:34:06.197 --> 00:34:10.967
You do realize, if you're wrong-
about the big picture, that is-

551
00:34:11.038 --> 00:34:12.973
you're going to burn, right?

552
00:34:13.042 --> 00:34:15.204
What do you want me to do-
just accept it, pack it in?

553
00:34:15.279 --> 00:34:18.739
Yeah. I want you to accept
that sometimes patients die
against all reason,

554
00:34:18.819 --> 00:34:20.754
and sometimes they get better
against all reason.

555
00:34:20.822 --> 00:34:23.314
No, they don't.
We just don't know the reason.

556
00:34:23.393 --> 00:34:26.090
I think the nuns
would agree with you on that.

557
00:34:31.240 --> 00:34:33.334
[Tapping]

558
00:34:35.281 --> 00:34:38.252
I just wanted to say that I know
that you did everything you could.

559
00:34:38.319 --> 00:34:41.654
I don't need verification from you
to know that I'm doing my job well.

560
00:34:41.725 --> 00:34:44.628
That's your problem, not mine.
I was just being nice.

561
00:34:44.697 --> 00:34:47.463
Yeah, well, you don't need
to always do that.

562
00:34:49.940 --> 00:34:51.806
Merry Christmas.

563
00:35:01.426 --> 00:35:04.795
Sister Augustine's been extubated.

564
00:35:07.102 --> 00:35:10.335
Good.
She's requested to check out,
against medical advice.

565
00:35:10.408 --> 00:35:12.343
She wants to go back
to the monastery.

566
00:35:12.411 --> 00:35:14.676
Well, talk her out of it.

567
00:35:14.749 --> 00:35:18.050
I think I may have
talked her into it.

568
00:35:20.092 --> 00:35:22.391
[Sighs]

569
00:35:34.917 --> 00:35:37.250
Room's paid up
for the rest of the week.

570
00:35:38.757 --> 00:35:40.692
Might as well stick around.

571
00:35:40.761 --> 00:35:45.030
This illness...
is a test of my faith.

572
00:35:45.101 --> 00:35:49.302
If it's his will to take me,
it doesn't matter where I am.

573
00:35:49.375 --> 00:35:52.106
I can accept that.

574
00:35:52.180 --> 00:35:54.581
Does anybody believe
anything you say?

575
00:35:56.487 --> 00:35:58.422
You're not accepting.

576
00:35:59.894 --> 00:36:01.829
You're running away.

577
00:36:01.897 --> 00:36:04.059
Just like you always do.

578
00:36:04.134 --> 00:36:06.969
You ran away from the monastery
to get laid.

579
00:36:08.241 --> 00:36:12.043
You ran away from the real world
when getting laid didn't
work out so good.

580
00:36:12.115 --> 00:36:15.917
Now things aren't working out again,
so off you go.

581
00:36:15.987 --> 00:36:19.925
Why is it so difficult for you
to believe in God?

582
00:36:19.994 --> 00:36:24.331
What I have difficulty with
is the whole concept of belief.

583
00:36:24.403 --> 00:36:26.872
Faith isn't based on logic
and experience.

584
00:36:26.940 --> 00:36:30.378
I experience God
on a daily basis...

585
00:36:30.446 --> 00:36:34.282
and the miracle of life all around-

586
00:36:34.353 --> 00:36:38.223
the miracle of birth,
the miracle of love.

587
00:36:38.293 --> 00:36:41.024
He is always with me.

588
00:36:41.098 --> 00:36:45.333
Where is the miracle in delivering
a crack-addicted baby?

589
00:36:45.406 --> 00:36:47.739
Hmm?

590
00:36:47.810 --> 00:36:51.248
Then watching her mother abandon her
'cause she needs another score.

591
00:36:51.315 --> 00:36:53.443
Miracle oflove.

592
00:36:53.520 --> 00:36:56.320
You're over twice as likely
to be killed...

593
00:36:56.391 --> 00:36:59.362
by the person you love
than by a stranger.

594
00:36:59.430 --> 00:37:02.629
Are you trying to talk me
out of my faith?

595
00:37:02.702 --> 00:37:06.538
You can have all the faith you want
in spirits and the afterlife...

596
00:37:06.608 --> 00:37:09.408
and heaven and hell.

597
00:37:09.480 --> 00:37:12.211
But when it comes to this world,
don't be an idiot.

598
00:37:13.387 --> 00:37:16.825
'Cause you can tell me
that you put your faith in God
to get you through the day,

599
00:37:16.893 --> 00:37:19.921
but when it comes time
to cross the road,
I know you look both ways.

600
00:37:19.998 --> 00:37:24.768
I don't believe he is inside me
and is going to save me.

601
00:37:24.841 --> 00:37:29.577
I believe he is inside me
whether I live or die.

602
00:37:29.648 --> 00:37:31.640
Then you might as well live.

603
00:37:33.589 --> 00:37:35.990
You got a better shot
betting on me than on him.

604
00:37:37.863 --> 00:37:40.560
When I was 15,

605
00:37:40.634 --> 00:37:45.131
I was on every kind of birth control
known to man-
[Gasps]

606
00:37:45.209 --> 00:37:48.544
And I still got pregnant.

607
00:37:48.615 --> 00:37:53.521
I blamed God. I hated him
for ruining my life.

608
00:37:53.590 --> 00:37:55.525
But then I realized something.

609
00:37:55.593 --> 00:38:01.229
You can't be angry with God
and not believe in him
at the same time.

610
00:38:01.303 --> 00:38:05.036
No one can.
Not even you, Dr. House.

611
00:38:10.219 --> 00:38:14.180
How'd it go?
She has God inside her.

612
00:38:14.259 --> 00:38:17.458
It would have been easier
to deal with a tumor.

613
00:38:17.531 --> 00:38:19.762
Maybe she's allergic to God?

614
00:38:24.777 --> 00:38:27.714
We've looked everywhere
for an allergen that could
be causing this reaction...

615
00:38:27.783 --> 00:38:29.877
except one place- inside her.

616
00:38:29.953 --> 00:38:33.322
On her medical history, she didn't
mention any surgery.
She had one.

617
00:38:33.392 --> 00:38:36.830
Can we get her records?
What hospital was it at?
She didn't have it at a hospital.

618
00:38:36.898 --> 00:38:39.994
Order a full body scan.
What if she refuses?

619
00:38:40.071 --> 00:38:43.600
Tell her I'm looking
for a miracle.

620
00:38:44.745 --> 00:38:47.716
[Foreman]
No piercings. No fillings.

621
00:38:47.783 --> 00:38:51.448
No surgical pins in the arm.
No implants.

622
00:38:51.523 --> 00:38:54.323
It's clean as a whistle.
What's House looking for?

623
00:38:55.897 --> 00:38:59.562
- What is that?
- Don't know.

624
00:38:59.638 --> 00:39:02.233
Lock on it.
Get a 3-D representation.

625
00:39:02.309 --> 00:39:04.437
[Typing]

626
00:39:07.417 --> 00:39:10.252
Oh, my God.

627
00:39:13.194 --> 00:39:17.759
The copper cross- a form of birth control
pulled off the market in the '80s.

628
00:39:17.835 --> 00:39:21.534
- So she's allergic to copper.
- Rare, but it happens.

629
00:39:21.609 --> 00:39:23.441
Wouldn't she know
she had an I.U.D.?

630
00:39:23.512 --> 00:39:26.004
She had an abortion.
I.U.D. Must have been left in,

631
00:39:26.083 --> 00:39:29.179
embedded in the endometrial tissue
where it couldn't be detected.

632
00:39:29.255 --> 00:39:32.385
So, all we have to do
is remove the I.U.D.

633
00:39:32.461 --> 00:39:34.760
Then the symptoms
should subside.

634
00:39:34.831 --> 00:39:39.533
I got this I.U.D. When I was 15.
It-It's been more than 20 years.

635
00:39:39.606 --> 00:39:42.702
Prolonged exposure to an allergen
with minimal symptoms.

636
00:39:42.778 --> 00:39:47.275
But at some point.
All it takes is one last contact
to cause a full-blown reaction.

637
00:39:47.353 --> 00:39:50.688
Just like a balloon filled with air-
one last breath, it explodes.

638
00:39:51.694 --> 00:39:55.063
The first time I got the rash
was when I was washing
the copper cookware.

639
00:39:55.133 --> 00:40:00.096
And all your subsequent symptoms
came from ingesting food prepared in it.

640
00:40:00.175 --> 00:40:02.667
Dr. House found his miracle.

641
00:40:02.747 --> 00:40:04.682
I doubt he'll interpret it that way.

642
00:40:04.750 --> 00:40:06.912
[Laughs]

643
00:40:06.987 --> 00:40:09.013
You told me your favorite passage.

644
00:40:09.090 --> 00:40:11.082
Would you like to hear mine?

645
00:40:13.332 --> 00:40:15.392
"Celebrate and be glad,

646
00:40:15.468 --> 00:40:18.405
because your brother was dead
and is alive again."

647
00:40:18.473 --> 00:40:21.444
The prodigal son.

648
00:40:21.512 --> 00:40:24.813
He'll be waiting for you
when you're ready.

649
00:40:26.654 --> 00:40:28.885
We'll schedule your surgery
for tomorrow.

650
00:40:35.937 --> 00:40:37.872
The sixth circle of hell.

651
00:40:37.940 --> 00:40:41.673
Confined in a sweat box
with a bloody nose,
and all the tissues are soggy.

652
00:40:41.747 --> 00:40:44.012
I think that's the seventh.
No. The seventh is-

653
00:40:44.084 --> 00:40:48.022
God, you must be fun at parties.
I think we both know
the flaw in that theory.

654
00:40:48.091 --> 00:40:51.585
How's the sister?
Heart rate is normal,
kidneys functioning.

655
00:40:51.664 --> 00:40:54.999
You know how it is with nuns.
You take out their I.U.D.'s,
they just bounce right back.

656
00:40:55.070 --> 00:40:57.437
Great.
Told you I didn't screw up.

657
00:40:59.077 --> 00:41:02.276
You screwed up.
I gave her.1 c.c. Of epinephrine.

658
00:41:02.349 --> 00:41:04.944
Yeah, and if Cuddy hadn't taken you
off the case, you would have killed her.

659
00:41:07.425 --> 00:41:10.396
You wanna come over
for Christmas dinner?

660
00:41:10.463 --> 00:41:13.901
You'reJewish.
Yeah. Hanukkah dinner.

661
00:41:13.970 --> 00:41:16.736
What do you care?
It's food. It's people.
No, thanks.

662
00:41:18.911 --> 00:41:23.351
Maybe I'll come to your place.
Your wife doesn't mind
being alone at Christmas?

663
00:41:23.419 --> 00:41:26.185
I'm a doctor.
She's used to being alone.

664
00:41:27.627 --> 00:41:29.687
I don't wanna talk about it.
Neither do I.

665
00:41:34.705 --> 00:41:36.731
You did good with the nun.

666
00:41:36.808 --> 00:41:41.544
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

667
00:41:41.617 --> 00:41:45.750
Merry Christmas, Dr. House.
Dr. Wilson.

668
00:41:47.060 --> 00:41:49.029
Good night.

669
00:41:50.700 --> 00:41:53.226
That was sweet.

